# Rest in Peace beside Planar Void (planar-void-lets-a-creature-die-then-exiles-it-and-leaves-earlier-cards-in-the-graveyard
# is the same game with Planar Void): Rest in Peace's "If a card or token would be put into a graveyard from anywhere,
# exile it instead" is a replacement effect (CR 614.1a), and "When Rest in Peace enters, exile all graveyards" empties
# them first. Bot1 Bolts Bot2 on turn 1 (17), then casts Rest in Peace on turn 3: its enters trigger exiles that Bolt.
# Bot2's Haywire Mite ("When this creature dies, you gain 2 life") is Bolted on turn 5: it goes straight to exile, so it
# never dies (CR 700.4) and Bot2 stays at 17, and nothing waits on the stack once the Bolt has resolved.

